# Next.js App Router Rules

## Page Files

- `page.tsx` files are thin wrappers — they import and compose components, nothing else.
- No business logic, no direct Convex calls, no complex JSX in page files.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD - app/chat/page.tsx
import ChatList from "@/components/chat/ChatList";

export default function ChatPage() {
  return <ChatList />;
}

// ❌ BAD - logic and UI mixed in page file
export default function ChatPage() {
  const conversations = useQuery(api.conversations.list);
  return (
    <div className="flex flex-col gap-4">
      {conversations?.map((c) => (
        <div key={c._id}>{c.name}</div>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Layout Files

- Root `layout.tsx` wraps the app with providers (`ConvexClientProvider`).
- Nested layouts handle feature-level chrome (sidebars, headers).
- Layouts NEVER fetch data — they provide structure only.

## ConvexClientProvider Setup

Place in `components/providers/ConvexClientProvider.tsx`:

```tsx
"use client";
import { ConvexProvider, ConvexReactClient } from "convex/react";
import { ReactNode } from "react";

const convex = new ConvexReactClient(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL!);

export default function ConvexClientProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  return <ConvexProvider client={convex}>{children}</ConvexProvider>;
}
```

## Loading & Error States

- Every route segment with async data should have `loading.tsx` with a skeleton UI.
- Every route segment should have `error.tsx` with a user-friendly error boundary.
- Use `not-found.tsx` for 404 states.

## Route Organization

- Use route groups `(groupName)` for layouts without affecting the URL.
- Use dynamic segments `[paramName]` for resource-based routes.
- Keep the route tree shallow — max 3 levels deep.

## Environment Variables

- Client-side Convex URL: `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL` in `.env.local`.
- NEVER commit `.env.local` — it is in `.gitignore`.
- NEVER hardcode secrets or URLs in source code.

## Metadata

- Define `metadata` export in each `page.tsx` or `layout.tsx` for SEO.

```tsx
export const metadata = {
  title: "Chat | Online Mafia",
  description: "Real-time chat",
};
```
